 • The task explicitly requires computing 3 * 7.                                
 • The computation must be performed using the run_python tool.                 
 • The final output must be only the numeric result (i.e., 21), with no extra   
   text, no repetition of tool calls, and no explanation.                       
 • No external data, files, dates, names, or contextual parameters are involved 
   — this is a pure arithmetic evaluation.                                      

1.2. Facts to look up                                                           

 • None. The expression 3 * 7 involves only literals known a priori; no external
   source (file, directory, regex, web resource, etc.) is referenced or         
   required.                                                                    
 • No tool documentation lookup is needed: the task explicitly mandates use of  
   run_python, and its interface is already provided in the tool list.          

1.3. Facts to derive                                                            

 • The integer value of 3 * 7, i.e., 21.                                        
 • This is a deterministic arithmetic derivation requiring no simulation or     
   approximation — just exact integer multiplication.                           
 • No intermediate facts (e.g., intermediate variables, time ranges, price      
   sequences) are involved; the derivation is direct and atomic.                

2. Plan                                                                         

 1 Use run_python to execute a minimal Python statement that computes 3 * 7 and 
   prints the result.                                                           
 2 Ensure the Python code outputs only the integer 21, with no additional       
   strings, formatting, or whitespace.                                          
 3 Capture the stdout from run_python, which will contain exactly 21.           
 4 Pass that raw numeric string directly to final_answer as the sole output.    ───────────────────────────────── Initial plan ─────────────────────────────────
